<section id="privacy">
  <div class="wrap legal">
    <div class="section-head" style="margin-bottom:0;">
      <div class="eyebrow">Legal</div>
      <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="legal-meta">
      <span><strong>Last updated:</strong> September 11, 2026</span>
      <span><strong>Applies to:</strong> the ReTrace iOS app</span>
      <span><strong>Data collected by the developer:</strong> none</span>
    </div>

    <div class="fact-row">
      <div class="fact"><div class="k">Account required</div><div class="v">No</div></div>
      <div class="fact"><div class="k">Network requests</div><div class="v">None — works in airplane mode</div></div>
      <div class="fact"><div class="k">Third‑party analytics or ads</div><div class="v">None</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose" style="max-width:none;">
      <h3>Overview</h3>
      <p>
        ReTrace is designed to work entirely on your device. It does not require an
        account, does not communicate with any server operated by us, and does not
        include advertising, analytics, or third‑party tracking software of any kind.
        This policy explains, plainly, what the small amount of data the app handles
        is used for and where it lives.
      </p>

      <h3>What ReTrace stores, and where</h3>
      <p>
        Everything you enter — projects, steps, parts, connections, notes, reference
        photos, and your app settings — is stored locally on your device using Apple's
        on‑device SwiftData framework. None of it is copied to iCloud by the app,
        uploaded to us, or shared with any third party. Uninstalling the app removes
        this data, and <strong>Settings → Delete All Data</strong> removes it at any
        time without uninstalling.
      </p>

      <h3>Camera and Photos</h3>
      <p>
        When you document a step, a photo you take or choose is saved only in the
        app's own local storage. A photo is always optional — a step can be recorded
        with just a type and a short note instead. Photos are never uploaded, and no
        image data is transmitted anywhere by the app.
      </p>

      <h3>Notifications</h3>
      <p>
        Restore reminders you choose to set are scheduled locally on your device using
        Apple's notification framework. They do not involve a push notification
        service or any server operated by us, and are only scheduled if you turn one
        on from a project.
      </p>

      <h3>Information we do not collect</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>No account, email address, or sign‑in of any kind</li>
        <li>No location data</li>
        <li>No advertising identifiers or tracking pixels</li>
        <li>No usage analytics, crash reports, or telemetry sent to us</li>
        <li>No data sold or shared with data brokers, advertisers, or other apps</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Children's privacy</h3>
      <p>
        ReTrace does not knowingly collect personal information from anyone, including
        children, because it does not collect personal information from its users at
        all — everything stays on the device.
      </p>

      <h3>Changes to this policy</h3>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the "Last updated" date above will change with it.
        Because the app has no account system, we cannot notify you individually —
        please check back here if you have questions about a new version.
      </p>

      <h3>Contact</h3>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy or how ReTrace handles data on your device can be
        sent to <a href="mailto:support@rtrace.xyz">support@rtrace.xyz</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

